---
import Callout from '../Callout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../CodeBlock.astro';
import StepCard from '../StepCard.astro';
---

<div class="sec" id="s6">
  <div class="num">06</div>
  <h2>First project: build yourself a website</h2>
  <p class="lede">Everything above, used once, end to end. Budget an hour.</p>
  <div class="steps">
    <StepCard number="1" title={'Set up the folder'}
      ><p>
        Make a folder called <code class="i">my-site</code>. Inside it, make a <code
          class="i">photos</code
        > folder with a few images and a <code class="i">bio.txt</code> file with
        a paragraph about you.
      </p></StepCard
    >
    <StepCard number="2" title={'Write the prompt with the prompt writer'}
      ><p>
        Open a normal Claude chat, paste the prompt writer from section two and
        answer its questions. You will end up with something like the prompt
        below. Copy it.
      </p></StepCard
    >
    <StepCard number="3" title={'Start a Delta thread'}
      ><p>
        Open <code class="i">my-site</code> in Delta, start a thread and paste the
        prompt. Read the plan it comes back with. If the plan mentions anything you
        did not ask for, say so. Then give it the ok.
      </p></StepCard
    >
    <StepCard number="4" title={'Review the build'}
      ><p>
        It should create <code class="i">index.html</code> and <code class="i"
          >style.css</code
        >. Open <code class="i">index.html</code> in your browser (double click it).
        Does it show your name, your bio and your photos? Comment in the thread on
        anything that is off and let it fix it. Accept when it is right.
      </p></StepCard
    >
    <StepCard number="5" title={'Tweak it yourself in Zed'}
      ><p>
        Open the folder in Zed, click <code class="i">index.html</code> and change
        a word in the bio. Save, refresh the browser. Then open <code class="i"
          >style.css</code
        >, find a line with a colour like <code class="i">#0a0f0b</code> and change
        it. Save, refresh. That is you editing code.
      </p></StepCard
    >
  </div>
  <CodeBlock
    label={'The prompt you will end up with'}
    code={"Goal: a one page personal website for NZB.\n\nContext: I am not a programmer. This folder is empty apart from a photos folder with my images and a bio.txt with a short paragraph about me.\n\nConstraints: one index.html file and one style.css file, no frameworks, no sign ups, no tracking. Dark background, big photos, easy to read on a phone. Do not change anything in the photos folder. Don't finish until you have checked that every photo in the photos folder shows on the page and the page has no broken links.\n\nWhat done looks like: I open index.html in my browser and see my name, the bio from bio.txt, all the photos in a grid and an email link at the bottom.\n\nOutput format: show me a short plan first and wait for my ok before writing files. When finished, tell me how to open the page.\n\nExample: the feel of a simple photographer portfolio page, mostly images, very little text."}
    copy
  />
  <Callout title={'Where to go next'}
    ><svg
      slot="icon"
      width="22"
      height="22"
      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
      fill="none"
      stroke="var(--color-b8ffd0)"
      stroke-width="2"
      stroke-linecap="round"
      stroke-linejoin="round"
      ><path d="M12 2v4"></path><path d="m16.2 7.8 2.9-2.9"></path><path
        d="M18 12h4"></path><path d="m16.2 16.2 2.9 2.9"></path><path
        d="M12 18v4"></path><path d="m4.9 19.1 2.9-2.9"></path><path d="M2 12h4"
      ></path><path d="m4.9 4.9 2.9 2.9"></path></svg
    ><p>
      Once the page exists, every new idea is a new thread. "Add a contact
      form", "make the photos open bigger when tapped", "add a page for my
      woodworking". Same loop each time: prompt writer, thread, plan, review,
      accept.
    </p></Callout
  >
  <Callout title={'It only exists on your machine for now'} warning
    ><svg
      slot="icon"
      width="22"
      height="22"
      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
      fill="none"
      stroke="var(--color-ffb347)"
      stroke-width="2"
      stroke-linecap="round"
      stroke-linejoin="round"
      ><path d="M12 9v4"></path><path d="M12 17h.01"></path><path
        d="M10.3 3.9 1.8 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.7 3h17a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3L13.7 3.9a2 2 0 0 0-3.4 0z"
      ></path></svg
    ><p>
      At this point the site is a folder on your computer. Nobody else can visit
      it. Getting it live on the internet needs hosting sorted, and that is a
      separate job with its own choices. I am leaving it out of this guide on
      purpose. When you have something you want people to see, tell me and we
      will sort it then.
    </p></Callout
  >
</div>
